Q) What is method hiding?
    Method hiding occurs when a subclass defines a 
    static method with the same signature as a 
    static method in its superclass.
Example:- class Parent {
    static void show() {
        System.out.println("Parent");
    }
}
class Child extends Parent {

    static void show() {
        System.out.println("Child");
    }
}
class Main {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        Parent p = new Child();

        p.show();
    }
}---------------------
Output
------------------
Parent

The static method is resolved based on the reference type, which is Parent.

Therefore:

Parent p = new Child();
        ↓
Reference type = Parent
Object type    = Child
        ↓
p.show()
        ↓
Parent.show()

This is method hiding, not method overriding.